  "content": {
    "id": "p26-group27-32-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find the range of the following functions.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p26-group27-32-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=3x+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$R=(-\\infty,\\infty)$",
          "worked": "The non-horizontal straight line extends indefinitely upward and downward, so every real $y$-value occurs.\n\n$R=(-\\infty,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-group27-32-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=x^2-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$R=[-1,\\infty)$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2&\\ge 0\\\\x^2-1&\\ge -1\\end{align*}$$\nThe minimum is $-1$, attained at $x=0$, and there is no upper bound.\n\n$R=[-1,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-group27-32-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=x^2+3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$R=[3,\\infty)$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2&\\ge 0\\\\x^2+3&\\ge 3\\end{align*}$$\nThe minimum is $3$, attained at $x=0$, and there is no upper bound.\n\n$R=[3,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-group27-32-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=4x^2-3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$R=[-3,\\infty)$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2&\\ge 0\\\\4x^2&\\ge 0\\\\4x^2-3&\\ge -3\\end{align*}$$\nThe minimum is $-3$, attained at $x=0$, and there is no upper bound.\n\n$R=[-3,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-group27-32-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=4-3x^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$R=(-\\infty,4]$",
          "worked": "Multiplication by a negative number reverses the inequality.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2&\\ge 0\\\\-3x^2&\\le 0\\\\4-3x^2&\\le 4\\end{align*}$$\nThe maximum is $4$, attained at $x=0$, and there is no lower bound.\n\n$R=(-\\infty,4]$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-group27-32-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=x^3-2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$R=(-\\infty,\\infty)$",
          "worked": "The cubic graph is continuous and extends indefinitely downward and upward. Translating it down by $2$ leaves every real $y$-value attainable.\n\n$R=(-\\infty,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      }
    ]
  },
